e, \"among other things, to break out, displace, replace the paradigm of race [America's enduring malaise].\" As Wideman puts it: \"Teach me who I might be, who you might be - without it.\". From affluent Amherst to blue-collar Pittsburgh to rural South Carolina, here is the story of an American family. Wresting himself free from the shackles of racial ideology, Wideman bravely engages not only the living but also the \"ghostlier demarcations\" of his family's past, the better to understand who he is today and to heal familial wounds. Fatheralong is a triumphant book of reckoning, an inspiring celebration of homecoming.","publicationYear":1994,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Biography","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fatheralong-a-meditation-on-fathers-sons-race-and-society-john-edgar-wideman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Race relations","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fatheralong-a-meditation-on-fathers-sons-race-and-society-john-edgar-wideman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Family","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fatheralong-a-meditation-on-fathers-sons-race-and-society-john-edgar-wideman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Fathers and sons","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fatheralong-a-meditation-on-fathers-sons-race-and-society-john-edgar-wideman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African American authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fatheralong-a-meditation-on-fathers-sons-race-and-society-john-edgar-wideman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"African American men","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-fatheralong-a-meditation-on-fathers-sons-race-and-society-john-edgar-wideman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"American Authors","sourceId":"source-open-library-